  "body": "Follow-up from the review of PR #3082 (#2965), comment 7051611241.\n\nThe first-traverse law judges an operation only when the machine kind is `Kind::Mill` (`is_mill` in `answers()`, `crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs`). On a mill-turn machine, the mill kinds (2D, 3D, vertical drilling, and since #2965 the multi-axis and rotary kinds) are not judged. #2901 left the same gap for the kinds that it judged.\n\nRisk: the first rapid of a mill operation on a mill-turn machine can start from an unknown X/Y and go through the stock, the chuck or the tailstock. No law refuses it.\n\nWork:\n1. Judge the mill kinds on a mill-turn machine with the same laws as on a mill. Use the steel of that machine (chuck, tailstock, turret) as the work-holding.\n2. Add pinning tests: one mill-turn case that is refused and one that is clear.\n\nRelated: #3077 (cross drill on a lathe or mill-turn machine).\n",
